@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;security] agents-postgres-authority
PostgreSQL is the authority for thread order, turn claims, executor fences and
tool outcomes. A live process, network connection or guest-supplied ID alone
MUST NOT authorize a state transition.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] agents-audit-content-free
Agent audit receipts and diagnostic events MUST contain only identifiers,
closed action kinds and outcomes. Prompts, titles, model content, command
arguments, tool output and credentials belong only in authorized thread data.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] agents-ambiguous-effect-no-replay
An issued tool command with an ambiguous result MUST become uncertain after
executor loss or VM execution change. It MUST NOT be dispatched again.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] agents-cli-browser-approval
CLI prompt authority MUST originate from an explicit authenticated browser
approval of a hash of the CLI's random secret. Marshall MUST store only that
hash, bind it to one VM and actor for a short lifetime, and recheck current VM
write access before every CLI mutation. An approval URL alone MUST NOT act as
a bearer credential.
